# PRE-REGISTRATION — LOCKED v1.0
## Blackwell Minerals Conservation Law: Full IMA/RRUFF Population Test
## and Boundary Mechanism Probes

Registration ID: [stamp at filing]
Registration date (UTC): [stamp at filing]
Population freeze: IMA Mineral List via RRUFF — record list version,
retrieval date, source URL, and SHA-256 of the frozen source file at filing.
No scientific parameter in this document may be altered after the freeze.
Any change requires a new version number and a new registration.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 1. THE CLAIM UNDER TEST

Seat function:
    seat(rho) = 18.319261532267927 + (1/4) * ln(rho / 5514)

Occupancy claim (Module A): every species admitted to the primary
crystallographic population (Section 3) has a reference-state
crystallographic density rho satisfying

    500.0957 <= rho <= 22604.3007   [kg/m^3]

equivalently seat in [17.7192, 18.671974].

Density is computed only as:
    rho = Z * M / (N_A * V_cell)
with V_cell the refined three-dimensional periodic unit-cell volume,
M the formula mass under the clauses of Section 2.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 2. LOCKED CLAUSES

C1. STANDARD STATE. Reference state is T = 293.15 K, P = 1 atm
    (101.325 kPa). Densities measured at other temperatures are
    corrected to 293.15 K using a stated volumetric thermal-expansion
    source. If no correction source exists and the measurement
    temperature differs from 293.15 K by more than 2 K, the species is
    TEMPERATURE-INDETERMINATE (not a falsifier, not a conformer).
    Exception: temperature-restricted crystalline species (e.g. ice Ih)
    are evaluated at the highest temperature at 1 atm at which the
    approved phase is stable (ice Ih: 273.15 K) and flagged T-RESTRICTED.

C2. TERRESTRIAL ISOTOPIC ABUNDANCE. M uses standard IUPAC terrestrial
    atomic weights. Synthetically isotopically enriched crystals are
    excluded from Module A. (They appear only in Module C.)

C3. ZEOLITIC CHANNEL OCCUPANCY. For microporous framework minerals,
    M includes extra-framework water at the stoichiometric content of
    the IMA-approved formula. If the approved formula states a range,
    the upper endpoint is used for the primary classification and the
    lower endpoint is reported as a sensitivity case. If the two
    endpoints change the classification, the species is
    HYDRATION-INDETERMINATE.

C4. CRYSTALLINITY. The primary population includes only species with a
    refined three-dimensional periodic unit cell. Amorphous mineraloids
    (e.g. opal, allophane), bulk porous aggregates (e.g. diatomite),
    liquids at the reference state (e.g. native mercury), and fully
    metamict phases lacking refined lattice parameters are excluded
    from Module A and listed by name in the exclusion register.
    Bulk/pycnometric densities are never admissible for classification;
    they may be reported as corroboration only.

C5. NO POST-HOC EXCLUSIONS. A species may be excluded only under
    C1–C4. Any exclusion decided after its density is known is a
    protocol deviation: it is logged, and the species is restored in a
    sensitivity analysis.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 3. POPULATION AND DATA HIERARCHY

Population: all IMA-approved species in the frozen RRUFF list
(> 6,200 species at drafting).

Admissible density evidence, in descending order:
  (1) single-crystal XRD refined cell + approved formula;
  (2) powder XRD Rietveld-refined cell + approved formula;
  (3) published calculated density traceable to (1) or (2).
Handbook bulk densities are inadmissible for classification.

Uncertainty: propagate V_cell, formula-mass (including hydration and
site-occupancy terms under C3), and atomic-weight uncertainties to a
95% confidence interval for rho for every species.

Reporting counts (all must be published):
  N_total (frozen list), N_primary (admitted under C1–C4),
  N_excluded (by clause, named), N_temperature-indeterminate,
  N_hydration-indeterminate, N_boundary-indeterminate,
  N_conforming, N_falsifying.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 4. CLASSIFICATION AND FALSIFICATION RULES (MODULE A)

CONFORMING: point estimate of rho inside [500.0957, 22604.3007].

BOUNDARY-INDETERMINATE: point estimate inside the band but the 95% CI
crosses a boundary, OR point estimate outside the band but the 95% CI
includes the band. Triggers independent remeasurement; counts neither
for nor against the claim.

FALSIFIED: at least one admitted species whose 95% CI lies ENTIRELY
outside the band (upper bound < 500.0957, or lower bound >
22604.3007), surviving the C1–C3 sensitivity cases. One such species
falsifies the occupancy claim as scoped. No re-banding, re-scoping, or
edge adjustment is permitted after the freeze.

SUPPORTED (as scoped): N_falsifying = 0 at the freeze, with all
indeterminate species reported. Support extends only to the frozen
population under these clauses.

Known edge context at registration (informational, not evidence):
  - Ceiling margin: pure osmium, accepted room-temperature X-ray
    density approx. 22,587 kg/m^3, sits 17.3 kg/m^3 (0.077%) below
    the ceiling. Osmium's classification must be computed from its
    refined cell under C1–C2, not adopted from a handbook value.
  - Floor buffer: lightest expected primary members are ice Ih
    (917 kg/m^3 at 273.15 K, T-RESTRICTED) and light organic minerals
    (approx. 1,010–1,090 kg/m^3), all > 400 kg/m^3 above the floor.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 5. MODULE C TARGET TABLES — BOUNDARY MECHANISM PROBES

Module C does NOT test occupancy and cannot falsify Module A.
It tests whether the ceiling behaves as a physical state boundary:
whether any independent observable changes at rho* = 22604.3007
kg/m^3 when the boundary is crossed at (nearly) constant chemistry.
Crossing variables are knobs; in-situ XRD density is the verdict.
A crossing counts only if the measured density 95% CI lies entirely
on the far side of rho*.

### 5.1 Iridium isotope series (constant-volume model; verify by XRD)
Anchor: natural Ir = 22,562 kg/m^3 at 293.15 K.
M(191Ir) = 190.960594 u; M(193Ir) = 192.962926 u;
natural mean (x = 0.627) = 192.216056 u.
rho(x) = 22562 * Mbar(x) / 192.216056.

  x(193Ir)   Mbar (u)    rho (kg/m^3)   delta vs rho*   seat       status
  0.000      190.960594  22414.64       -189.66         18.669867  below
  0.250      191.461177  22473.39       -130.91         18.670522  below
  0.500      191.961760  22532.15       -72.15          18.671175  below
  0.627      192.216056  22562.00       -42.30          18.671506  below (natural)
  0.750      192.462343  22590.91       -13.39          18.671826  below
  0.806980   192.576435  22604.3007     0               18.671974  CROSSOVER
  0.850      192.662576  22614.41       +10.11          18.672086  above
  0.900      192.762693  22626.16       +21.86          18.672216  above
  1.000      192.962926  22649.67       +45.37          18.672475  above

Target specimens: x = 0.75, 0.79, 0.807, 0.82, 0.85, 1.00, each with
mass-spectrometric enrichment assay and single-crystal XRD density.
Sensitivity: a +/-10 kg/m^3 error in the natural-Ir anchor moves the
predicted crossover by approx. -/+4.3 percentage points of 193Ir;
classify only from measured specimen density.

### 5.2 Osmium pressure trajectory (isothermal, 293.15 K)
Anchor: natural Os = 22,587 kg/m^3 at 293.15 K, 1 atm.
rho*/rho0 = 1.000765958; ln(rho*/rho0) = 0.000765665.
Third-order Birch–Murnaghan, K0' = 4:

  K0 (GPa)   crossover pressure (GPa)
  350        0.268
  395        0.303
  400        0.307   (nominal design point)
  462        0.354

(If the alternate anchor Os = 22,590 kg/m^3 is ever adopted, the
nominal point becomes 0.253 GPa; the anchor must be locked before
any run and the other value retired for this protocol.)

### 5.3 Osmium temperature trajectory (isobaric, 1 atm)
Constant-alpha_V model, T_cross = 293.15 - 0.000765665 / alpha_V:

  alpha_V (1/K)   cooling (K)   T_cross (K)
  14.0e-6         54.69         238.46
  15.3e-6         50.04         243.11   (nominal)
  17.0e-6         45.04         248.11

Experimental search window: 238–248 K, by cryo-XRD measurement of
rho(T); the constant-alpha point is a target, not a classification.

### 5.4 Combined osmium P–T crossover line (nominal model)
P_cross(T) = 400 * [0.000765665 + 15.3e-6 * (T - 293.15)] GPa
(K0 = 400 GPa, alpha_V = 15.3e-6 /K):

  T (K)     P_cross (GPa)
  373.15    0.796
  323.15    0.490
  298.15    0.337
  293.15    0.306
  273.15    0.184
  253.15    0.061
  243.11    0.000  (crosses on cooling alone, nominal model)

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 6. MODULE C ENDPOINTS AND DECISION RULES

Pre-registered observables at each crossing: equation-of-state
parameters (K0, K0'), phonon response (Debye temperature / phonon
density of states / Raman mode frequencies), and, as secondary
readouts, cohesive energy per atom and electrical resistivity.
Hardness and bulk conductivity are excluded as primary endpoints.

MECHANISM SUPPORTED requires ALL of:
  (a) a discontinuity, kink, or change point in at least one primary
      observable located at rho* within the combined density
      uncertainty;
  (b) the effect reproduced on at least two independent crossing
      paths (isotope, pressure, temperature, alloying);
  (c) the filed boundary outperforming placebo boundaries at
      0.95, 0.99, 1.01, and 1.05 x rho* in the pre-registered model
      comparison, out of sample.

MECHANISM NOT SUPPORTED: all primary observables cross rho* smoothly
on all paths, or effects track pressure / temperature / isotope mass
rather than density. This outcome does not falsify Module A; it
establishes that seat functions as a density coordinate, and the
occupancy band stands or falls by Module A alone.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 7. DEVIATIONS AND REPORTING

All deviations from this document are logged with date and reason and
published with the results. Results are reported for the full frozen
population and all Module C specimens, including null, indeterminate,
and falsifying outcomes. No interim peeking at classification counts
before the freeze is complete.

END OF LOCKED PRE-REGISTRATION v1.0